; A name may end in a backslash. The generated assembly carries names in
; comments, and the C preprocessor that reads it joins a line ending in a
; backslash to the next, which took the instruction after such a name with
; it (on both targets). Comments now write the backslash as an escape.

(defun f (x\) (let y\ (+ x\ 1)) (pprint y\) (* y\ 2))
(pprint 'a\)
(pprint 'b)
(f 20)
